  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Making Home(s) in Displacement (2021), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 3 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 3,323 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Making Home(s) in Displacement by Luce Beeckmans, Alessandra Gola, Ashika Singh and others was published by Leuven University Press in 2021. Conceptually, the work connects to Scholarship, Refugee, Displaced person, Sociology and Geopolitics.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 3 citations. Citations peaked in 2024 with 2 citing works. Notable citing venues include Gender Place & Culture, Planning Perspectives and Wellbeing Space and Society. They come from 3 countries, led by Belgium, Finland and Turkey.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 3,323 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Sustainable cities and communities among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven and Research Foundation Flanders (FWO).</p>",
